{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Forms often edit data loaded from an API. A server-state library such as\nTanStack Query should own fetching, caching, loading, and retries; TanStack Form\nshould own the editable copy."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"There are two supported ways to provide async initial values: wait to create\nthe form until the data is ready, or create it immediately with complete\nfallback values. Choose the approach that best matches the loading experience\nyour UI needs."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"wait-for-data-before-creating-the-editor","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wait for data before creating the editor"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Render a loading or error state first, then mount a component whose\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" are complete."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<!-- UserPage.vue -->\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { toRef } from 'vue'\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/vue-query'\nimport UserEditor from './UserEditor.vue'\nimport type { User } from './types.ts'\n\nconst props = defineProps<{ userId: string }>()\nconst userId = toRef(props, 'userId')\nconst {\n  data: user,\n  isPending,\n  isError,\n} = useQuery({\n  queryKey: ['user', userId],\n  queryFn: async (): Promise<User> => {\n    const response = await fetch(`/api/users/${userId.value}`)\n    return response.json()\n  },\n})\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <p v-if=\"isPending\">Loading…</p>\n  <p v-else-if=\"isError\" role=\"alert\">Could not load the user.</p>\n  <UserEditor v-else-if=\"user\" :key=\"userId\" :user=\"user\" />\n</template>","lang":"vue"},{"type":"code","value":"<!-- UserEditor.vue -->\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { useForm } from '@tanstack/vue-form'\nimport type { User } from './types.ts'\n\nconst props = defineProps<{ user: User }>()\nconst form = useForm({\n  defaultValues: props.user,\n  onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n    await fetch('/api/users', {\n      method: 'PUT',\n      headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },\n      body: JSON.stringify(value),\n    })\n  },\n})\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <form @submit.prevent=\"form.handleSubmit()\">\n    <!-- fields -->\n  </form>\n</template>","lang":"vue"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This pattern is useful when no form state is needed during loading. Mounting\nthe editor only after data exists also makes it explicit when switching records\nshould create a fresh form. The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":":key"},{"type":"text","value":" recreates the editor when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"userId"},{"type":"text","value":"\nchanges."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"create-the-form-before-data-arrives","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create the form before data arrives"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can instead call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useForm"},{"type":"text","value":" in the same component as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQuery"},{"type":"text","value":". Provide a\nstatic, shape-complete fallback so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" are never "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":", then\nupdate a reactive options object when data arrives."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { reactive, toRef, watchEffect } from 'vue'\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/vue-query'\nimport { useForm } from '@tanstack/vue-form'\nimport type { User } from './types.ts'\n\nconst props = defineProps<{ userId: string }>()\nconst userId = toRef(props, 'userId')\nconst emptyUser: User = {\n  firstName: '',\n  lastName: '',\n}\n\nconst {\n  data: user,\n  isPending,\n  isError,\n} = useQuery({\n  queryKey: ['user', userId],\n  queryFn: async (): Promise<User> => {\n    const response = await fetch(`/api/users/${userId.value}`)\n    return response.json()\n  },\n})\n\nconst formOptions = reactive({\n  defaultValues: emptyUser,\n  onSubmit: async ({ value }: { value: User }) => {\n    await fetch('/api/users', {\n      method: 'PUT',\n      headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },\n      body: JSON.stringify(value),\n    })\n  },\n})\n\nwatchEffect(() => {\n  if (user.value) {\n    formOptions.defaultValues = user.value\n  }\n})\n\nconst form = useForm(formOptions)\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <p v-if=\"isPending\">Loading…</p>\n  <p v-else-if=\"isError\" role=\"alert\">Could not load the user.</p>\n  <form v-else @submit.prevent=\"form.handleSubmit()\">\n    <!-- fields -->\n  </form>\n</template>","lang":"vue"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Vue adapter observes the reactive options object. When query data replaces\nthe fallback, TanStack Form applies the new "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" to untouched fields\nwhile preserving fields the user has already touched. In this example, the\nfields remain unmounted during loading, so the user cannot edit them before the\nloaded values arrive. You can also render the empty form immediately when that\nbetter suits the UI."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"background-refetches-and-record-changes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Background refetches and record changes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" establish the form's baseline; they are not a fully controlled\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"values"},{"type":"text","value":" prop. In the fallback pattern, later "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" updates use the\nsame touched-field-preserving behavior."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If background refetches arrive while a user is editing, decide at the product\nlevel whether to keep local edits, prompt before replacing them, or call\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.reset(nextValues)"},{"type":"text","value":" deliberately. Do not overwrite in-progress input\nmerely because a query refreshed."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When switching to a different record, either remount a keyed editor as in the\nfirst pattern or deliberately reset the existing form. Otherwise, touched\nvalues from the previous record can be preserved when the new defaults arrive."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"wait-for-data-before-creating-the-editor","text":"Wait for data before creating the editor","level":2},{"id":"create-the-form-before-data-arrives","text":"Create the form before data arrives","level":2},{"id":"background-refetches-and-record-changes","text":"Background refetches and record changes","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nForms often edit data loaded from an API. A server-state library such as\nTanStack Query should own fetching, caching, loading, and retries; TanStack Form\nshould own the editable copy.\n\nThere are two supported ways to provide async initial values: wait to create\nthe form until the data is ready, or create it immediately with complete\nfallback values. Choose the approach that best matches the loading experience\nyour UI needs.\n\n## Wait for data before creating the editor\n\nRender a loading or error state first, then mount a component whose\n`defaultValues` are complete.\n\n```vue\n<!-- UserPage.vue -->\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { toRef } from 'vue'\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/vue-query'\nimport UserEditor from './UserEditor.vue'\nimport type { User } from './types.ts'\n\nconst props = defineProps<{ userId: string }>()\nconst userId = toRef(props, 'userId')\nconst {\n  data: user,\n  isPending,\n  isError,\n} = useQuery({\n  queryKey: ['user', userId],\n  queryFn: async (): Promise<User> => {\n    const response = await fetch(`/api/users/${userId.value}`)\n    return response.json()\n  },\n})\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <p v-if=\"isPending\">Loading…</p>\n  <p v-else-if=\"isError\" role=\"alert\">Could not load the user.</p>\n  <UserEditor v-else-if=\"user\" :key=\"userId\" :user=\"user\" />\n</template>\n```\n\n```vue\n<!-- UserEditor.vue -->\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { useForm } from '@tanstack/vue-form'\nimport type { User } from './types.ts'\n\nconst props = defineProps<{ user: User }>()\nconst form = useForm({\n  defaultValues: props.user,\n  onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n    await fetch('/api/users', {\n      method: 'PUT',\n      headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },\n      body: JSON.stringify(value),\n    })\n  },\n})\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <form @submit.prevent=\"form.handleSubmit()\">\n    <!-- fields -->\n  </form>\n</template>\n```\n\nThis pattern is useful when no form state is needed during loading. Mounting\nthe editor only after data exists also makes it explicit when switching records\nshould create a fresh form. The `:key` recreates the editor when `userId`\nchanges.\n\n## Create the form before data arrives\n\nYou can instead call `useForm` in the same component as `useQuery`. Provide a\nstatic, shape-complete fallback so `defaultValues` are never `undefined`, then\nupdate a reactive options object when data arrives.\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { reactive, toRef, watchEffect } from 'vue'\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/vue-query'\nimport { useForm } from '@tanstack/vue-form'\nimport type { User } from './types.ts'\n\nconst props = defineProps<{ userId: string }>()\nconst userId = toRef(props, 'userId')\nconst emptyUser: User = {\n  firstName: '',\n  lastName: '',\n}\n\nconst {\n  data: user,\n  isPending,\n  isError,\n} = useQuery({\n  queryKey: ['user', userId],\n  queryFn: async (): Promise<User> => {\n    const response = await fetch(`/api/users/${userId.value}`)\n    return response.json()\n  },\n})\n\nconst formOptions = reactive({\n  defaultValues: emptyUser,\n  onSubmit: async ({ value }: { value: User }) => {\n    await fetch('/api/users', {\n      method: 'PUT',\n      headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },\n      body: JSON.stringify(value),\n    })\n  },\n})\n\nwatchEffect(() => {\n  if (user.value) {\n    formOptions.defaultValues = user.value\n  }\n})\n\nconst form = useForm(formOptions)\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <p v-if=\"isPending\">Loading…</p>\n  <p v-else-if=\"isError\" role=\"alert\">Could not load the user.</p>\n  <form v-else @submit.prevent=\"form.handleSubmit()\">\n    <!-- fields -->\n  </form>\n</template>\n```\n\nThe Vue adapter observes the reactive options object. When query data replaces\nthe fallback, TanStack Form applies the new `defaultValues` to untouched fields\nwhile preserving fields the user has already touched. In this example, the\nfields remain unmounted during loading, so the user cannot edit them before the\nloaded values arrive. You can also render the empty form immediately when that\nbetter suits the UI.\n\n## Background refetches and record changes\n\n`defaultValues` establish the form's baseline; they are not a fully controlled\n`values` prop. In the fallback pattern, later `defaultValues` updates use the\nsame touched-field-preserving behavior.\n\nIf background refetches arrive while a user is editing, decide at the product\nlevel whether to keep local edits, prompt before replacing them, or call\n`form.reset(nextValues)` deliberately. Do not overwrite in-progress input\nmerely because a query refreshed.\n\nWhen switching to a different record, either remount a keyed editor as in the\nfirst pattern or deliberately reset the existing form. Otherwise, touched\nvalues from the previous record can be preserved when the new defaults arrive.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: async-initial-values\ntitle: Async Initial Values\n---\n\nForms often edit data loaded from an API. A server-state library such as\nTanStack Query should own fetching, caching, loading, and retries; TanStack Form\nshould own the editable copy.\n\nThere are two supported ways to provide async initial values: wait to create\nthe form until the data is ready, or create it immediately with complete\nfallback values. Choose the approach that best matches the loading experience\nyour UI needs.\n\n## Wait for data before creating the editor\n\nRender a loading or error state first, then mount a component whose\n`defaultValues` are complete.\n\n```vue\n<!-- UserPage.vue -->\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { toRef } from 'vue'\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/vue-query'\nimport UserEditor from './UserEditor.vue'\nimport type { User } from './types.ts'\n\nconst props = defineProps<{ userId: string }>()\nconst userId = toRef(props, 'userId')\nconst {\n  data: user,\n  isPending,\n  isError,\n} = useQuery({\n  queryKey: ['user', userId],\n  queryFn: async (): Promise<User> => {\n    const response = await fetch(`/api/users/${userId.value}`)\n    return response.json()\n  },\n})\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <p v-if=\"isPending\">Loading…</p>\n  <p v-else-if=\"isError\" role=\"alert\">Could not load the user.</p>\n  <UserEditor v-else-if=\"user\" :key=\"userId\" :user=\"user\" />\n</template>\n```\n\n```vue\n<!-- UserEditor.vue -->\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { useForm } from '@tanstack/vue-form'\nimport type { User } from './types.ts'\n\nconst props = defineProps<{ user: User }>()\nconst form = useForm({\n  defaultValues: props.user,\n  onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n    await fetch('/api/users', {\n      method: 'PUT',\n      headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },\n      body: JSON.stringify(value),\n    })\n  },\n})\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <form @submit.prevent=\"form.handleSubmit()\">\n    <!-- fields -->\n  </form>\n</template>\n```\n\nThis pattern is useful when no form state is needed during loading. Mounting\nthe editor only after data exists also makes it explicit when switching records\nshould create a fresh form. The `:key` recreates the editor when `userId`\nchanges.\n\n## Create the form before data arrives\n\nYou can instead call `useForm` in the same component as `useQuery`. Provide a\nstatic, shape-complete fallback so `defaultValues` are never `undefined`, then\nupdate a reactive options object when data arrives.\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { reactive, toRef, watchEffect } from 'vue'\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/vue-query'\nimport { useForm } from '@tanstack/vue-form'\nimport type { User } from './types.ts'\n\nconst props = defineProps<{ userId: string }>()\nconst userId = toRef(props, 'userId')\nconst emptyUser: User = {\n  firstName: '',\n  lastName: '',\n}\n\nconst {\n  data: user,\n  isPending,\n  isError,\n} = useQuery({\n  queryKey: ['user', userId],\n  queryFn: async (): Promise<User> => {\n    const response = await fetch(`/api/users/${userId.value}`)\n    return response.json()\n  },\n})\n\nconst formOptions = reactive({\n  defaultValues: emptyUser,\n  onSubmit: async ({ value }: { value: User }) => {\n    await fetch('/api/users', {\n      method: 'PUT',\n      headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },\n      body: JSON.stringify(value),\n    })\n  },\n})\n\nwatchEffect(() => {\n  if (user.value) {\n    formOptions.defaultValues = user.value\n  }\n})\n\nconst form = useForm(formOptions)\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <p v-if=\"isPending\">Loading…</p>\n  <p v-else-if=\"isError\" role=\"alert\">Could not load the user.</p>\n  <form v-else @submit.prevent=\"form.handleSubmit()\">\n    <!-- fields -->\n  </form>\n</template>\n```\n\nThe Vue adapter observes the reactive options object. When query data replaces\nthe fallback, TanStack Form applies the new `defaultValues` to untouched fields\nwhile preserving fields the user has already touched. In this example, the\nfields remain unmounted during loading, so the user cannot edit them before the\nloaded values arrive. You can also render the empty form immediately when that\nbetter suits the UI.\n\n## Background refetches and record changes\n\n`defaultValues` establish the form's baseline; they are not a fully controlled\n`values` prop. In the fallback pattern, later `defaultValues` updates use the\nsame touched-field-preserving behavior.\n\nIf background refetches arrive while a user is editing, decide at the product\nlevel whether to keep local edits, prompt before replacing them, or call\n`form.reset(nextValues)` deliberately. Do not overwrite in-progress input\nmerely because a query refreshed.\n\nWhen switching to a different record, either remount a keyed editor as in the\nfirst pattern or deliberately reset the existing form. Otherwise, touched\nvalues from the previous record can be preserved when the new defaults arrive.\n"}
